lse, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/smoke-1016/omp36-opus/omp-36/cells/with/trig-omp-reported/1/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/ee4a1d48b77fe5de548078d29f9a22c4d4608a91/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n**Cause:** the fixed format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` had nothing to match the trailing `Z` (the UTC marker), so `strptime` stopped with \"unconverted data remains: Z\".\n\n**Fix:** the function now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead. On Python 3.11 and later, which covers the 3.13.5 installed here, it accepts a trailing `Z` and still handles timestamps without one.\n\n**Behaviour changes to be aware of:**\n- **Timezone-aware results:** a timestamp ending in `Z` or `+HH:MM` now comes back with UTC or that offset attached. Timestamps without one still come back as before, with no timezone. Code that compares the two kinds directly will raise a `TypeError`.\n- **Looser input:** it now accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as a date alone (`\"2026-10-12\"`) or fractional seconds. The old version rejected these.\n- **Python version:** on Python older than 3.11, `fromisoformat` rejects `Z`. You'd need to replace the trailing `Z` with `+00:00` before parsing.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read":